1
00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:03.649
[S01] All right, hello and welcome to this training.

2
00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:09.029
[S01] As you can see from the title, what we're going to be covering today is how to achieve anything by ignoring reality.

3
00:00:09.039 --> 00:00:14.490
[S01] And as you can see from the overview, what we're going to be discussing more specifically is first the overview itself.

4
00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:20.750
[S01] The backwards equation, seeing the equation, flipping the variables, holding the inversion through the lag, the review,

5
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:23.589
[S01] and then your action items for the day or the next few days.

6
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:28.329
[S01] With that said, and out of the way, let's get started and talk about the backwards equation.

7
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:34.770
[S01] So what I want to walk you through today is something that genuinely changed how I think about pretty much everything.

8
00:00:34.859 --> 00:00:41.829
[S01] And it starts with a really simple observation that there is an equation underneath our lives, underneath our money,

9
00:00:42.159 --> 00:00:44.170
[S01] our health, our relationships, all of it.

10
00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:49.969
[S01] And the thing is, most of us have read it backwards for as long as we can remember,

11
00:00:49.979 --> 00:00:53.570
[S01] which means every decision you've made and every pattern you've fallen into

12
00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:56.530
[S01] has been built on a sequence that was inverted from the start.

13
00:00:56.560 --> 00:01:00.829
[S01] And once you see that, once you really get it, and I believe you will after this training,

14
00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.469
[S01] a lot of things that never made really a lot of sense before suddenly click into place.

15
00:01:05.959 --> 00:01:10.170
[S01] So here's how the equation runs for most people.

16
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:15.769
[S01] And this probably describes your default mode as well, and it describes almost everyone's.

17
00:01:15.799 --> 00:01:20.170
[S01] And the way it plays out is really something happens in your external world, in your reality.

18
00:01:20.760 --> 00:01:25.069
[S01] Your mind then immediately generates a thought about it, that thought produces a feeling.

19
00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:30.069
[S01] You act from that feeling, and then those actions produce more of the same kind of reality,

20
00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:33.370
[S01] which triggers the same thoughts and the same feelings again.

21
00:01:33.659 --> 00:01:36.870
[S01] And so the whole thing just loops over and over and over again,

22
00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:39.670
[S01] without you ever noticing that you're the one keeping it going.

23
00:01:40.099 --> 00:01:45.209
[S01] And the reason it's so hard to catch is that the whole sequence really happens on autopilot.

24
00:01:45.219 --> 00:01:49.129
[S01] Like you wake up, you check your phone, maybe you see something that stresses you out,

25
00:01:49.459 --> 00:01:52.469
[S01] and then a thought fires before you're even really conscious of it.

26
00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:57.170
[S01] And it can be anything. It can be, "This isn't good," or "I'm falling behind."

27
00:01:57.260 --> 00:02:01.170
[S01] And then that thought instantly produces a response in your body, a feeling.

28
00:02:01.859 --> 00:02:07.469
[S01] It could be a tightness in your chest, it could be a low hum of anxiety that just sits there for the rest of the day.

29
00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:14.969
[S01] And from that place, you then start making decisions, you start interacting with people in reality and making, and make choices,

30
00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:17.870
[S01] and you carry that energy into everything essentially,

31
00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:22.240
[S01] which is how you end up at the end of most days feeling like nothing has really changed.

32
00:02:22.259 --> 00:02:28.530
[S01] You spent the entire day reacting to circumstances that were already old, already finished,

33
00:02:28.539 --> 00:02:31.569
[S01] already the output of a previous cycle,

34
00:02:31.599 --> 00:02:37.110
[S01] and then you use those old outputs as the raw material for your next round of thinking and feeling.

35
00:02:37.460 --> 00:02:40.770
[S01] So of course, the result looks the same.

36
00:02:41.259 --> 00:02:46.009
[S01] And the really tricky part is that none of this really feels like a choice.

37
00:02:46.039 --> 00:02:51.069
[S01] It feels like just how life works, which is exactly why most people never really question it.

38
00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:57.229
[S01] And it keeps running the same in the background, the same loop for years or even decades,

39
00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.469
[S01] without people really realizing there's another way to operate.

40
00:03:02.060 --> 00:03:08.569
[S01] And the thing is, the whole sequence feels so obvious and so natural that nobody ever stops to question it.

41
00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:12.389
[S01] Of course, you think negative thoughts when bad things happen, right?

42
00:03:12.400 --> 00:03:17.310
[S01] Of course, those thoughts make you feel a certain way, and then of course, you react from that place.

43
00:03:17.659 --> 00:03:20.030
[S01] You're just reacting to the world, right?

44
00:03:20.039 --> 00:03:23.370
[S01] Of course, that's just being a reasonable person, right?

45
00:03:23.860 --> 00:03:25.669
[S01] But that right there is the trap.

46
00:03:25.930 --> 00:03:32.870
[S01] What you're actually doing when you're on that sequence is really letting the output of your life dictate the input.

47
00:03:33.530 --> 00:03:37.139
[S01] And when you do that, you're locked into producing the same result every time.

48
00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:41.430
[S01] So it's sort of like being stuck in a feedback loop

49
00:03:41.439 --> 00:03:45.330
[S01] where the answer keeps feeding back into the question,

50
00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:49.229
[S01] and the question keeps producing the same answer, and on and on it goes.

51
00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:54.129
[S01] And you just go around and around, wondering why your life feels like it's on repeat,

52
00:03:54.159 --> 00:03:59.469
[S01] when the mechanism causing the repetition is something you're doing every single day without awareness.

53
00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:03.469
[S01] And every time you let your circumstances trigger the same automatic thoughts,

54
00:04:03.599 --> 00:04:06.870
[S01] which produce the same feelings, which drive the same reactions,

55
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:12.969
[S01] you're basically telling your system, "Yes, this is real, this is important, keep, keep building more of this."

56
00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:18.329
[S01] Which means your reactions are reinforcing the very reality you're trying to change.

57
00:04:18.360 --> 00:04:21.889
[S01] And that's why willpower alone can't really break the cycle.

58
00:04:21.889 --> 00:04:26.069
[S01] The cycle is running at a deeper level than willpower can actually reach.

59
00:04:26.329 --> 00:04:32.860
[S01] So whatever you're looking at right now in your life, maybe it's your bank account, maybe it's your body,

60
00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:37.579
[S01] maybe it's your relationships, all of that is basically a printout, right?

61
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:38.910
[S01] Just like the image shows.

62
00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.509
[S01] And I mean that in a very literal sense.

63
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:47.569
[S01] It's the result of an equation that was already solved weeks or months or even years ago

64
00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.110
[S01] by the thoughts you were thinking and the feelings you were carrying at that time,

65
00:04:51.759 --> 00:04:55.509
[S01] which means the reality you're experiencing today is old data.

66
00:04:56.120 --> 00:05:01.410
[S02] It's already finished and it has nothing to do with what's actually possible for you going forward.

67
00:05:01.949 --> 00:05:07.379
[S02] So think of your current circumstances as a kind of energetic history, a record of

68
00:05:07.709 --> 00:05:10.290
[S02] where your internal state was at some earlier point.

69
00:05:10.529 --> 00:05:16.079
[S02] And the reason that matters is that most people look at that record and they treat it like it's a live feed.

70
00:05:16.649 --> 00:05:24.209
[S02] They think this is what's happening right now, when really it's more like reading last month's report and mistaking it for today's one.

71
00:05:24.839 --> 00:05:31.439
[S02] So basically, there is a delay between when you change internally and when that change shows up externally.

72
00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.339
[S02] And it's built in, it's a built in feature of how all of this works.

73
00:05:35.339 --> 00:05:39.600
[S02] So if you're judging your progress by what you can see in front of you right now,

74
00:05:39.629 --> 00:05:43.620
[S02] you're always going to be looking at evidence from an older version of yourself,

75
00:05:43.649 --> 00:05:47.339
[S02] which is genuinely misleading if you don't understand the mechanics.

76
00:05:47.399 --> 00:05:54.180
[S02] So the stuff that's showing up in your life today is residual, is the echo of a previous internal state,

77
00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.079
[S02] is the echo of a cause that was a long time ago.

78
00:05:58.350 --> 00:06:02.699
[S02] And the sooner you really internalize that, the sooner you stop giving it so much weight,

79
00:06:02.939 --> 00:06:06.829
[S02] because you realize you're reading the receipt from a transaction that has already happened

80
00:06:07.319 --> 00:06:11.970
[S02] and that that receipt tells you nothing about what the next transaction is going to look like, the better.

81
00:06:13.579 --> 00:06:18.959
[S02] So this is actually a really freeing thing, once you really understand it.

82
00:06:18.959 --> 00:06:26.250
[S02] It means your current reality isn't a verdict, it isn't some final judgment on who you are or what you're capable of.

83
00:06:26.459 --> 00:06:31.800
[S02] And I know most of you probably know this to a degree, it's just the tail end of an older process.

84
00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:37.199
[S02] You, you know that your future is probably brighter than your current reality,

85
00:06:37.949 --> 00:06:44.370
[S02] but you most likely don't know that the current reality is just a result of what happened maybe years ago.

86
00:06:44.850 --> 00:06:50.639
[S02] It's just the, as I said, the tail end of an older process and the equation that produced it has already been solved,

87
00:06:50.879 --> 00:06:55.050
[S02] which means you're free to write a completely new one, starting right now.

88
00:06:55.079 --> 00:07:01.290
[S02] And what comes out the other side of that new equation will most likely look nothing like what you're seeing today,

89
00:07:01.709 --> 00:07:04.949
[S02] which is honestly one of the most liberating realizations you can have.

90
00:07:04.980 --> 00:07:08.490
[S02] It takes the pressure off of your current situation entirely.

91
00:07:08.819 --> 00:07:12.629
[S02] And you stop fighting what's in front of you and you stop trying to fix the printout

92
00:07:12.779 --> 00:07:16.769
[S02] and instead you put all of your energy into writing better inputs,

93
00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:19.649
[S02] which is the only thing that actually moves the needle.

94
00:07:20.279 --> 00:07:25.290
[S02] And that shift from fixing the output to changing the input is basically the whole game.

95
00:07:25.709 --> 00:07:31.800
[S02] It's what separates people who stay stuck in the same patterns from people who seem to create change almost effortlessly.

96
00:07:32.149 --> 00:07:36.779
[S02] So the second group figured out that you don't change your life by wrestling with reality.

97
00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:40.230
[S02] You change it by changing what goes into the equation first.

98
00:07:40.800 --> 00:07:45.839
[S02] So the default equation, the one that almost everyone is running unconsciously,

99
00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:51.959
[S02] runs in a loop of circumstances, create thoughts, those thoughts create feelings, those feelings create some actions,

100
00:07:52.110 --> 00:07:54.779
[S02] and then those lead to the same circumstances.

101
00:07:54.930 --> 00:08:00.689
[S02] And that's a closed loop, there's no exit point, you just keep cycling through the same sequence over and over and over again.

102
00:08:00.779 --> 00:08:04.560
[S02] And the reason it feels so inescapable is that at every point in the chain,

103
00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:08.790
[S02] the next step feels like the only logical response to the one before it.

104
00:08:09.089 --> 00:08:13.139
[S02] So it never occurs to you that the whole chain could be reversed, right?

105
00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:18.810
[S02] And what makes this especially hard to see is that the default equation feels like reality itself.

106
00:08:19.079 --> 00:08:21.810
[S02] It feels like this is just how cause and effect works.

107
00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:28.860
[S02] Most people never really question it, they just assume that the outside world causes their thoughts and feelings and that's that.

108
00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:35.639
[S02] And then they spend their whole lives trying to rearrange the external circumstances, hoping it will make them feel different,

109
00:08:35.909 --> 00:08:42.269
[S02] which sometimes works temporarily, but never really lasts because the underlying equation hasn't changed.

110
00:08:42.779 --> 00:08:48.720
[S02] And a big part of why this is so ingrained is that you are conditioned into it from a very young age.

111
00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:53.309
[S02] Your parents and your teachers and culture all modeled the default equation for you.

112
00:08:53.370 --> 00:08:59.220
[S02] They taught you implicitly, mostly, that your thoughts and feelings are caused by what happens to you,

113
00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:03.000
[S02] which set up the whole pattern before you were old enough to even question it.

114
00:09:03.389 --> 00:09:09.629
[S02] So by the time you're an adult, running the default equation feels like, feels natural, it's as natural as breathing.

115
00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:15.090
[S02] You don't even register it as a pattern, let alone a pattern that you could actually change,

116
00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:20.820
[S02] which is why the first step in breaking out of it is simply becoming aware that it actually exists.

117
00:09:20.850 --> 00:09:23.399
[S02] You can't invert something you haven't even noticed.

118
00:09:23.789 --> 00:09:27.629
[S02] And what I'm telling you is that this whole chain is running in the wrong direction.

119
00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.350
[S02] The actual order is the reverse of what you've been taught.

120
00:09:31.740 --> 00:09:36.000
[S02] And the moment you understand that, the moment you really get that thoughts and feelings come first

121
00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:42.090
[S02] and reality follows and that you ignore reality and just create thoughts and feelings,

122
00:09:42.409 --> 00:09:47.100
[S02] everything starts to make a different kind of sense and you start to see why some people seem to create results

123
00:09:47.340 --> 00:09:52.100
[S02] almost magnetically, while others grind away for years and barely move the needle.

124
00:09:52.909 --> 00:09:58.649
[S02] So the inverted equation, the one that actually produces change, flips the order to thoughts.

125
00:09:59.000 --> 00:10:02.889
[S03] Create feelings, create actions which create new circumstances.

126
00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:08.190
[S03] And the key difference is that in this version, you're absolutely ignoring reality.

127
00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:13.470
[S03] You're the one choosing the starting point instead of letting your environment choose it for you,

128
00:10:13.629 --> 00:10:15.740
[S03] which puts you back in control of the whole chain.

129
00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:17.759
[S03] And that's what this whole training is really about.

130
00:10:17.769 --> 00:10:21.330
[S03] It's about learning to run the equation in the right direction.

131
00:10:21.529 --> 00:10:24.759
[S03] And the three steps I'm going to walk you through are the practical tools

132
00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:28.480
[S03] for actually doing it in your daily life, starting with the most fundamental one,

133
00:10:28.629 --> 00:10:31.740
[S03] which is simply learning to see the equation in the first place.

134
00:10:32.070 --> 00:10:34.840
[S03] Now, the reason most people's lives feel like they're on repeat,

135
00:10:35.029 --> 00:10:39.070
[S03] like the same problems keep cycling back around, no matter what they do,

136
00:10:39.230 --> 00:10:42.960
[S03] is because they keep looking at the old printout and using it as the input

137
00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:48.779
[S03] for the next round of thinking and feeling, which just produces another version of the same printout.

138
00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.840
[S03] And then they look at that one and they react to it again,

139
00:10:52.259 --> 00:10:55.200
[S03] and do the whole thing over and over and over again.

140
00:10:55.210 --> 00:11:00.009
[S03] And you can run that loop for decades, honestly, without ever realizing that you're the one sustaining it.

141
00:11:01.049 --> 00:11:05.000
[S03] And it's worth pointing out that this applies to everything, not just money or career stuff.

142
00:11:05.009 --> 00:11:08.799
[S03] It shows up in your relationships where you keep attracting the same kind of person

143
00:11:08.820 --> 00:11:10.190
[S03] or the same kind of dynamic.

144
00:11:10.360 --> 00:11:13.789
[S03] It shows up in health, where you keep falling back into the same patterns,

145
00:11:13.799 --> 00:11:16.230
[S03] no matter how many diets or programs you try.

146
00:11:16.389 --> 00:11:18.360
[S03] And it shows up in your general mood and energy,

147
00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:22.200
[S03] because all of those things are outputs of the same underlying equation.

148
00:11:22.529 --> 00:11:25.360
[S03] So if you've ever had that feeling of, here we go again,

149
00:11:25.559 --> 00:11:29.470
[S03] that sense that you're basically dealing with the same issue in a slightly different costume,

150
00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:33.500
[S03] that's the default equation doing exactly what it was designed to do,

151
00:11:33.860 --> 00:11:37.230
[S03] which is produce consistent results based on a consistent input.

152
00:11:37.580 --> 00:11:40.850
[S03] And the input hasn't changed because you've been letting the output write it.

153
00:11:41.129 --> 00:11:43.980
[S03] And once you see this pattern in one area of your life,

154
00:11:44.190 --> 00:11:47.700
[S03] you'll be able to start seeing it everywhere, because it really is universal.

155
00:11:48.009 --> 00:11:50.820
[S03] It's the same mechanism playing out across every domain,

156
00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:55.799
[S03] which is both a little overwhelming at first, but also incredibly empowering.

157
00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.990
[S03] There's one thing to fix, one equation to invert,

158
00:11:59.309 --> 00:12:02.100
[S03] and that inversion ripples out across everything else.

159
00:12:02.779 --> 00:12:06.129
[S03] And I want to be clear, this isn't about blaming yourself, right?

160
00:12:06.139 --> 00:12:09.190
[S03] When you understand that you've been running the equation backwards,

161
00:12:09.480 --> 00:12:13.870
[S03] yes, the natural response might be a little bit of frustration or guilt.

162
00:12:14.259 --> 00:12:17.070
[S03] But that's the old equation trying to reassert itself.

163
00:12:17.259 --> 00:12:21.669
[S03] The much more useful response is to just go, okay, now I see it and now I can change it.

164
00:12:21.679 --> 00:12:29.149
[S03] Almost as if you just finally got the answer to a mathematical equation, to a math problem,

165
00:12:29.679 --> 00:12:31.909
[S03] which is exactly what we're going to do in the next section.

166
00:12:31.919 --> 00:12:34.059
[S03] And it's really that mechanical.

167
00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:37.070
[S03] It's just a sequence that can be run in one direction or another.

168
00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:40.460
[S03] And most people happen to be running it in the direction that keeps them stuck.

169
00:12:40.789 --> 00:12:44.500
[S03] And once you learn to run it in the other direction, the results change.

170
00:12:44.509 --> 00:12:48.220
[S03] And they change in ways that feel almost surprising at first,

171
00:12:48.230 --> 00:12:50.360
[S03] because you're so used to the old output.

172
00:12:50.820 --> 00:12:54.850
[S03] And that's honestly the thing I want you to walk away with from this section,

173
00:12:55.059 --> 00:12:57.750
[S03] that the reason your life maybe looks a certain way,

174
00:12:58.690 --> 00:13:02.730
[S03] or the way it does look right now, is completely understandable.

175
00:13:02.740 --> 00:13:06.169
[S03] It's completely explainable and completely changeable,

176
00:13:06.179 --> 00:13:11.149
[S03] because it's all just the output of an equation, and equations can be rewritten.

177
00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:14.950
[S03] So with that said, let's cover seeing the equation.

178
00:13:15.379 --> 00:13:20.789
[S03] So before you can actually flip anything around, you have to actually see what's happening.

179
00:13:21.399 --> 00:13:28.269
[S03] The default equation runs so automatically, so far below the surface of your conscious awareness,

180
00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:31.830
[S03] that most people go through their entire day reacting to reality

181
00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:35.059
[S03] without once catching themselves in the act.

182
00:13:35.820 --> 00:13:39.730
[S03] And that automatic quality is exactly what gives it so much power,

183
00:13:40.389 --> 00:13:44.659
[S03] since you can't really change a process you haven't even identified yet.

184
00:13:45.389 --> 00:13:49.559
[S03] And what I mean by seeing the equation is honestly pretty straightforward.

185
00:13:49.570 --> 00:13:53.539
[S03] It's just starting to pay attention to the specific moments in your day

186
00:13:53.549 --> 00:13:57.159
[S03] where your external circumstances are dictating how you think

187
00:13:57.360 --> 00:13:59.950
[S03] and how that thinking is shaping how you feel.

188
00:13:59.980 --> 00:14:04.070
[S03] And then recognizing that in those moments, you're running the old sequence.

189
00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.230
[S03] You're letting the printout write the next equation.

190
00:14:07.519 --> 00:14:10.750
[S03] You're basically feeding the answer back into the formula,

191
00:14:10.929 --> 00:14:14.820
[S03] which is exactly the mechanism that keeps the loop locked into place.

192
00:14:15.269 --> 00:14:19.820
[S03] So for example, let's say you check your bank balance and it's lower than you want.

193
00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:24.960
[S03] A thought fires instantly, most likely, something like, I'm not where I should be,

194
00:14:25.509 --> 00:14:27.759
[S03] or I spent too much last weekend.

195
00:14:28.429 --> 00:14:31.019
[S03] And that thought drops something in your body, right?

196
00:14:31.029 --> 00:14:32.659
[S03] That heaviness, that tightness.

197
00:14:33.159 --> 00:14:36.669
[S03] And the whole thing happens in half a second, completely on autopilot,

198
00:14:36.789 --> 00:14:39.580
[S03] without you making any conscious choice about it.

199
00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:43.639
[S03] And from that lowered state, you go about your day carrying that weight

200
00:14:43.649 --> 00:14:46.139
[S03] into every conversation and every decision you make.

201
00:14:46.929 --> 00:14:50.100
[S03] And the speed of it is part of what makes it so invisible.

202
00:14:58.279 --> 00:15:04.279
[S04] The equation has already run and now you're living inside the output of that reaction,

203
00:15:04.309 --> 00:15:07.740
[S04] making it feel like the emotional state is just the truth,

204
00:15:07.769 --> 00:15:12.179
[S04] when really it was generated by a mechanical process you didn't even notice.

205
00:15:12.740 --> 00:15:15.039
[S04] And this happens dozens of times today, honestly.

206
00:15:15.070 --> 00:15:17.080
[S04] Not just with money, but with everything.

207
00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:22.200
[S04] Someone says something dismissive and maybe your mind interprets it in a certain way

208
00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:23.740
[S04] that shifts your mood.

209
00:15:23.940 --> 00:15:26.740
[S04] Or you see someone on social media doing better than you

210
00:15:26.769 --> 00:15:30.470
[S04] and a thought fires that contracts something inside.

211
00:15:31.039 --> 00:15:33.440
[S04] Or maybe you hit a setback in your work

212
00:15:33.639 --> 00:15:38.039
[S04] and the story your mind tells about it drops your whole energy.

213
00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:42.639
[S04] And each one of those moments is basically an instance of the default equation firing.

214
00:15:42.940 --> 00:15:47.269
[S04] And each one reinforces the loop that keeps your reality looking the same.

215
00:15:48.070 --> 00:15:52.080
[S04] And the thing about these micro reactions is that they accumulate.

216
00:15:52.110 --> 00:15:55.669
[S04] So even if no single one of them seems like a big deal,

217
00:15:55.940 --> 00:16:00.879
[S04] by the end of the day, you basically run the default equation fifty or a hundred times

218
00:16:00.909 --> 00:16:01.980
[S04] without catching it.

219
00:16:02.169 --> 00:16:06.139
[S04] And all of those reactions have collectively set the emotional tone

220
00:16:06.169 --> 00:16:08.980
[S04] that's going to shape what shows up next in your life.

221
00:16:09.340 --> 00:16:12.940
[S04] Which is why awareness alone, or just the act of starting to notice,

222
00:16:12.970 --> 00:16:15.379
[S04] is so much more powerful than it sounds on the surface,

223
00:16:15.409 --> 00:16:18.379
[S04] because every time you catch the thought mid-flight,

224
00:16:18.669 --> 00:16:20.840
[S04] you're interrupting a compounding process.

225
00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.179
[S04] You're pulling back one brick out of the wall

226
00:16:23.210 --> 00:16:25.470
[S04] that the default equation is trying to build.

227
00:16:25.870 --> 00:16:30.669
[S04] And over time, those interruptions add up to a fundamentally different internal landscape, right?

228
00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:35.039
[S04] Now, here's a useful way to really think about your recurring problems.

229
00:16:35.669 --> 00:16:38.980
[S04] They're kind of like background apps running on your phone.

230
00:16:39.570 --> 00:16:41.840
[S04] They're just sitting there quietly, they consume energy,

231
00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:43.480
[S04] and every time you open one of them,

232
00:16:43.509 --> 00:16:46.580
[S04] every time you give it your attention and your emotional investment,

233
00:16:46.740 --> 00:16:50.840
[S04] you're telling the system, "Keep this one active, this one really matters."

234
00:16:50.970 --> 00:16:53.440
[S04] And it stays in the loop, which is why some issues

235
00:16:53.639 --> 00:16:57.169
[S04] seem to follow you around for years, even when you think you've dealt with them.

236
00:16:58.210 --> 00:17:01.440
[S04] And you only have so much emotional bandwidth in a given day.

237
00:17:01.669 --> 00:17:04.680
[S04] And if half of it is going to background processes

238
00:17:04.710 --> 00:17:06.480
[S04] that are just recycling old patterns,

239
00:17:06.509 --> 00:17:10.740
[S04] then you have that much less available for actually creating something new.

240
00:17:11.039 --> 00:17:15.170
[S04] Which is why people often feel exhausted even when they haven't really done anything.

241
00:17:15.329 --> 00:17:19.440
[S04] Their internal system was busy running old equations all day long.

242
00:17:19.769 --> 00:17:22.329
[S04] So one of the most powerful moves you can actually make,

243
00:17:22.369 --> 00:17:26.670
[S04] and this sounds almost too simple, is to just stop opening the app.

244
00:17:26.940 --> 00:17:30.269
[S04] Meaning, stop engaging with the old pattern when it pops up.

245
00:17:30.299 --> 00:17:34.740
[S04] Let it sit there without clicking on it, and eventually it times out on its own.

246
00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:37.539
[S04] These patterns can only sustain themselves

247
00:17:37.569 --> 00:17:40.940
[S04] when you keep feeding them your attention and your emotional energy.

248
00:17:41.069 --> 00:17:44.279
[S04] And this is really the same principle we talked about earlier with the printout.

249
00:17:44.309 --> 00:17:48.339
[S04] The idea that your current reality is sustained by ongoing input.

250
00:17:48.470 --> 00:17:54.470
[S04] So when you withdraw the input, which in practical terms means withdrawing your emotional reactivity,

251
00:17:54.740 --> 00:17:57.140
[S04] the pattern starts to lose its hope, it starts to fade,

252
00:17:57.170 --> 00:17:59.440
[S04] because there's nothing feeding it anymore.

253
00:18:00.039 --> 00:18:01.839
[S04] And what you're really learning to do here

254
00:18:01.869 --> 00:18:05.980
[S04] is really become more selective about what gets your cognitive and emotional energy.

255
00:18:06.009 --> 00:18:09.670
[S04] Because right now, most people are just broadcasting their energy

256
00:18:09.710 --> 00:18:11.779
[S04] at whatever's loudest in their environment,

257
00:18:11.809 --> 00:18:15.779
[S04] or whatever's most urgent, or most stressful, or most in their face.

258
00:18:15.809 --> 00:18:18.440
[S04] And that's how the default equation stays in control.

259
00:18:18.470 --> 00:18:23.740
[S04] So the shift is really learning how to consciously choose where your energy goes

260
00:18:24.369 --> 00:18:27.140
[S04] instead of letting circumstances make that choice for you.

261
00:18:27.940 --> 00:18:30.339
[S04] And this doesn't mean suppressing your feelings

262
00:18:30.369 --> 00:18:32.140
[S04] or pretending things don't bother you.

263
00:18:32.170 --> 00:18:34.069
[S04] That's a different thing entirely, right?

264
00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.839
[S04] What it means is developing the ability to notice a thought rising

265
00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:40.740
[S04] and then choosing whether to invest in it or let it pass,

266
00:18:40.769 --> 00:18:42.740
[S04] which is a skill, it takes practice.

267
00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.539
[S04] And it gets easier the more you do it.

268
00:18:45.569 --> 00:18:50.980
[S04] And honestly, this is probably the most underrated skill in personal development, I think.

269
00:18:51.009 --> 00:18:54.980
[S04] Everyone wants the advanced techniques and the big breakthroughs,

270
00:18:55.009 --> 00:18:59.940
[S04] but the ability to simply notice your own thinking in real time and choose differently

271
00:19:00.069 --> 00:19:02.470
[S04] is the foundation that everything else is built on.

272
00:19:02.740 --> 00:19:05.140
[S04] Because without, none of the other steps really work.

273
00:19:05.369 --> 00:19:09.470
[S04] You have to do that in one way or another in order to create change.

274
00:19:09.940 --> 00:19:12.380
[S04] So, the practical move here,

275
00:19:12.410 --> 00:19:15.069
[S04] and this is something you can start doing literally today,

276
00:19:15.240 --> 00:19:17.269
[S04] is what I call the equation check.

277
00:19:17.369 --> 00:19:20.880
[S04] And all it takes is a few times a day, you just pause for a second

278
00:19:20.910 --> 00:19:25.170
[S04] and ask yourself, "Am I reacting to my reality right now, or am I creating it?"

279
00:19:26.130 --> 00:19:27.980
[S04] That's it, that one question.

280
00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:31.769
[S04] Because the moment you catch the thought that's driving your reaction,

281
00:19:32.000 --> 00:19:35.000
[S04] you've already stepped outside the loop for just a second.

282
00:19:35.130 --> 00:19:39.470
[S04] And that second of awareness is where the inversion becomes possible.

283
00:19:40.170 --> 00:19:43.440
[S04] Now, the pause itself is the thing, really.

284
00:20:04.339 --> 00:20:06.700
[S05] Between stimulus and response, there is a space.

285
00:20:06.710 --> 00:20:10.259
[S05] And in that space is your freedom and your power to choose.

286
00:20:10.289 --> 00:20:12.849
[S05] And that's essentially what the equation check is designed to give you.

287
00:20:12.859 --> 00:20:16.390
[S05] It's a tool for creating that space reliably multiple times a day.

288
00:20:16.400 --> 00:20:20.650
[S05] So that you're not just hoping for moments of awareness, but actively generating them.

289
00:20:21.309 --> 00:20:25.859
[S05] And consistency matters here more than intensity, as with a lot of things in life.

290
00:20:25.890 --> 00:20:31.700
[S05] Meaning it's much better to do three or four brief equation checks spread throughout your day

291
00:20:31.730 --> 00:20:37.220
[S05] than to do one big meditation in the morning and then run on autopilot for the next 16 hours.

292
00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:40.410
[S05] Because the default equation fires all day long.

293
00:20:40.440 --> 00:20:44.140
[S05] So your awareness practice needs to be distributed across the day too.

294
00:20:44.869 --> 00:20:49.619
[S05] And every time you do this, every time you catch the automatic thought in the middle of firing

295
00:20:49.630 --> 00:20:55.720
[S05] and then you pause, you're essentially weakening the automacity of the default equation just a little bit.

296
00:20:55.750 --> 00:21:00.990
[S05] And over days and weeks, those small disruptions accumulate into something really significant.

297
00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:06.559
[S05] Because the loop that's been running your life can only maintain itself really through uninterrupted repetition.

298
00:21:06.589 --> 00:21:09.970
[S05] Each interruption is chipping away at its foundation.

299
00:21:10.690 --> 00:21:14.920
[S05] And the results are cumulative in a way that's easy to underestimate at first.

300
00:21:14.940 --> 00:21:19.559
[S05] Because on any given day, the equation check might feel small and unremarkable.

301
00:21:19.589 --> 00:21:25.259
[S05] But if you do it consistently for a few weeks, you'll start to notice that your baseline emotional state has shifted.

302
00:21:25.289 --> 00:21:30.650
[S05] That you're less reactive generally, that things that used to hook you just don't land the same way.

303
00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:32.970
[S05] And that's the default equation losing its grip.

304
00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:37.420
[S05] And this is really the foundational practice for everything that comes next.

305
00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:43.799
[S05] Because without this ability to see the equation and interrupt it, the other two steps won't stick.

306
00:21:43.829 --> 00:21:47.859
[S05] You'll try to invert things, but the default pattern will keep pulling you back.

307
00:21:48.269 --> 00:21:53.319
[S05] So treat this step as the ground floor and give it the attention it really deserves.

308
00:21:53.349 --> 00:21:57.720
[S05] And look, I want to be honest with you about why this is difficult.

309
00:21:57.730 --> 00:21:58.940
[S05] And it should be.

310
00:21:58.970 --> 00:22:04.420
[S05] Your nervous system is literally built to read reality first and then respond second.

311
00:22:04.450 --> 00:22:06.259
[S05] It's a survival mechanism.

312
00:22:06.660 --> 00:22:09.730
[S05] And it has kept humans alive for hundreds of thousands of years.

313
00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:14.259
[S05] And you're asking it to operate in a way that feels fundamentally counterintuitive.

314
00:22:14.289 --> 00:22:18.990
[S05] Which is why it takes real practice and patience and a willingness to be bad at it for a while

315
00:22:19.009 --> 00:22:20.960
[S05] before it starts to become more natural.

316
00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:26.799
[S05] Because survival mode and creation mode, I believe, are genuinely two different ways of being.

317
00:22:27.430 --> 00:22:32.319
[S05] And your body defaults to survival because that's what kept your ancestors alive.

318
00:22:32.349 --> 00:22:36.339
[S05] So when you start trying to override that default, there's going to be resistance.

319
00:22:36.349 --> 00:22:37.960
[S05] There's going to be discomfort.

320
00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:42.700
[S05] And your system is most likely going to protest because it thinks you're doing something dangerous.

321
00:22:42.730 --> 00:22:43.140
[S05] Right?

322
00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:46.200
[S05] Even though you're actually just doing something that will change your life.

323
00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:48.460
[S05] And the wiring of this goes deep.

324
00:22:48.490 --> 00:22:51.579
[S05] It isn't some minor habit that you can just decide to stop.

325
00:22:51.609 --> 00:22:56.500
[S05] It's a neurological pattern that's been reinforced by every experience you've ever had.

326
00:22:56.529 --> 00:22:59.079
[S05] And you're not going to catch every reaction right away.

327
00:22:59.089 --> 00:23:02.220
[S05] And that's completely fine for the perfectionist sound there.

328
00:23:02.250 --> 00:23:05.940
[S05] The goal is to just catch more of them over time on average.

329
00:23:05.970 --> 00:23:09.000
[S05] And the trend matters infinitely more than any single instance.

330
00:23:09.329 --> 00:23:14.220
[S05] So be patient with the process and trust that even catching yourself one or two extra times a day

331
00:23:14.250 --> 00:23:16.539
[S05] or a week is meaningful progress.

332
00:23:16.569 --> 00:23:19.599
[S05] Because each catch is a small proof of concept and it shows that

333
00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:23.140
[S05] that the default equation can be actually interrupted.

334
00:23:23.490 --> 00:23:26.990
[S05] And that you're not completely at the mercy of your reactions.

335
00:23:27.000 --> 00:23:32.299
[S05] And that alone will start to shift something fundamental in how you relate to your own experience.

336
00:23:32.630 --> 00:23:38.940
[S05] So really, what you're doing with this whole first step is building the capacity to override a system

337
00:23:38.970 --> 00:23:43.420
[S05] that's been running unchecked your entire life, which is a big deal if you think about it.

338
00:23:43.450 --> 00:23:45.759
[S05] And it's worth acknowledging that rather than rushing through it.

339
00:23:45.789 --> 00:23:49.420
[S05] Because the people who take this step seriously and really practice it

340
00:23:49.430 --> 00:23:52.500
[S05] are the ones who make the other two steps work better.

341
00:23:52.970 --> 00:23:57.019
[S05] The people who skip it or treat it as obvious are the ones who end up back in the same loop

342
00:23:57.029 --> 00:23:59.380
[S05] six months later, wondering what happened.

343
00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:04.299
[S05] So think of this as the foundation, the thing that everything else really rests on.

344
00:24:04.690 --> 00:24:07.059
[S05] And give it the weight it deserves in your daily practice.

345
00:24:07.069 --> 00:24:11.259
[S05] Because if you can consistently see the equation firing in real time,

346
00:24:11.289 --> 00:24:14.059
[S05] you've already done something that most people never managed to do.

347
00:24:14.529 --> 00:24:18.000
[S05] And from that place of awareness, the inversion becomes genuinely possible.

348
00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:24.619
[S05] And once you've built this awareness muscle up to the point where you're catching yourself regularly throughout the day,

349
00:24:24.650 --> 00:24:27.259
[S05] where the equation check has become almost second nature,

350
00:24:27.789 --> 00:24:31.700
[S05] that's when you're ready for the second step, which is where things really start to get interesting.

351
00:24:31.710 --> 00:24:36.410
[S05] Because now you're going to take that awareness and use it to actually flip the variables around.

352
00:24:36.440 --> 00:24:39.059
[S05] So let's talk about flipping the variables.

353
00:24:39.890 --> 00:24:44.660
[S05] Now, once you see the equation running, the next move is to really invert it.

354
00:24:44.680 --> 00:24:47.619
[S05] And this is where the whole thing starts to get really interesting.

355
00:24:47.630 --> 00:24:50.759
[S05] Because what you're doing here is deliberately choosing the thoughts

356
00:24:50.779 --> 00:24:56.059
[S05] and generating the feelings of the reality you want before any evidence of it shows up in your life.

357
00:24:56.089 --> 00:25:00.279
[S05] And honestly, this is the step that most people either skip entirely or do halfway.

358
00:25:00.299 --> 00:25:06.180
[S05] And it's one that matters the most because this is where the actual direction of the equation really changes.

359
00:25:06.210 --> 00:25:08.660
[S05] So here's what I mean in practical terms.

360
00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:12.059
[S05] In the default equation, you wait for something good to happen.

361
00:25:12.089 --> 00:25:15.099
[S05] Your mind thinks a thought about it and then you feel good about it.

362
00:25:15.119 --> 00:25:17.740
[S05] That's the normal order that everyone's used to.

363
00:25:24.410 --> 00:25:27.059
[S06] That's just the normal order that everyone's used to.

364
00:25:27.089 --> 00:25:31.619
[S06] But in the inverted equation, you choose the thought first, which generates the feeling.

365
00:25:31.650 --> 00:25:35.420
[S06] You create the internal state deliberately and on purpose.

366
00:25:35.450 --> 00:25:38.410
[S06] And then you let reality reorganize around that.

367
00:25:38.440 --> 00:25:42.220
[S06] So you're writing the input side of the equation by hand.

368
00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:45.900
[S06] Instead of letting your circumstances fill it, you know, fill it in for you,

369
00:25:45.930 --> 00:25:48.809
[S06] which completely changes what comes out on the other end.

370
00:25:49.690 --> 00:25:54.730
[S06] Now, the key word here is first, because the timing is everything, right?

371
00:25:54.759 --> 00:25:59.009
[S06] You're not thinking, empowering thoughts and feeling good in response to something good that happened.

372
00:25:59.039 --> 00:26:01.529
[S06] You're generating them before anything has changed,

373
00:26:02.210 --> 00:26:05.369
[S06] which can feel counterintuitive and even a little crazy at first.

374
00:26:05.400 --> 00:26:06.970
[S06] But that's exactly the inversion.

375
00:26:07.000 --> 00:26:07.769
[S06] That's the whole point.

376
00:26:07.799 --> 00:26:11.819
[S06] You're reversing the direction of cause and effect in your own experience.

377
00:26:11.849 --> 00:26:13.089
[S06] And it has to be deliberate.

378
00:26:13.119 --> 00:26:16.140
[S06] It has to be something you do on purpose with intention.

379
00:26:16.170 --> 00:26:21.769
[S06] Because your default system is always going to want to read reality first and then respond second,

380
00:26:21.799 --> 00:26:24.890
[S06] which is why this step requires active practice.

381
00:26:25.490 --> 00:26:29.480
[S06] Often, you can't just hope your thoughts and feelings will change on their own.

382
00:26:29.509 --> 00:26:32.480
[S06] You have to actually choose them, which is a very different thing.

383
00:26:32.970 --> 00:26:38.170
[S06] So you can see the image of the default equation and the inverted equation.

384
00:26:38.759 --> 00:26:40.529
[S06] And there's a real reason this works, by the way.

385
00:26:40.559 --> 00:26:43.259
[S06] It's grounded in something your nervous system actually does.

386
00:26:43.289 --> 00:26:47.289
[S06] Your brain at a neurological level genuinely cannot tell the difference

387
00:26:47.319 --> 00:26:53.009
[S06] between a vividly felt internal experience and the one that's actually happening in the external world.

388
00:26:53.039 --> 00:26:57.299
[S06] So if you really sit with the thoughts and feelings of financial security, for example,

389
00:26:57.329 --> 00:27:01.809
[S06] if you let your body relax into um how you would think at that point

390
00:27:01.839 --> 00:27:05.809
[S06] and what that would feel like in your chest and your shoulders and your breathing,

391
00:27:05.839 --> 00:27:10.930
[S06] then your nervous system responds to that signal the same way it would respond to a real event.

392
00:27:11.329 --> 00:27:14.009
[S06] Because your biology doesn't fact check the source.

393
00:27:14.490 --> 00:27:17.480
[S06] It just processes whatever that data it receives.

394
00:27:17.809 --> 00:27:22.730
[S06] And there's a substantial body of research on this in neuroscience.

395
00:27:22.759 --> 00:27:29.220
[S06] The basic finding that being that mental rehearsal activates many of the same neural pathways

396
00:27:29.250 --> 00:27:34.529
[S06] as actual experience, which is why athletes use visualization so effectively.

397
00:27:34.930 --> 00:27:36.970
[S06] And it's the same mechanism at work here.

398
00:27:37.849 --> 00:27:41.329
[S06] Except instead of rehearsing a physical performance,

399
00:27:41.450 --> 00:27:44.609
[S06] you're rehearsing a cognitive and emotional state.

400
00:27:45.609 --> 00:27:49.740
[S06] So when you sit in the morning and genuinely feel into the state of the person

401
00:27:49.769 --> 00:27:54.480
[S06] who already has what you want, your biology is responding to that as if it's real.

402
00:27:55.250 --> 00:27:56.799
[S06] Your hormones most likely will shift.

403
00:27:56.829 --> 00:27:59.210
[S06] Your nervous system will calibrate to that frequency.

404
00:27:59.240 --> 00:28:03.009
[S06] And your whole physiology will start to align with a different reality.

405
00:28:03.359 --> 00:28:09.250
[S06] And that physiological shift is what changes the input of the equation at the most fundamental level.

406
00:28:10.130 --> 00:28:13.410
[S06] Now, the beautiful thing about this is that your body doesn't argue with it.

407
00:28:13.440 --> 00:28:17.890
[S06] It doesn't say, well, actually, you don't have that yet, so I'm not going to respond.

408
00:28:18.210 --> 00:28:22.329
[S06] It just processes the signal, which means you have the ability to manually set

409
00:28:22.359 --> 00:28:25.809
[S06] your internal state regardless of what's happening outside of you.

410
00:28:26.170 --> 00:28:28.170
[S06] And that's the inversion in action.

411
00:28:28.809 --> 00:28:32.650
[S06] So the morning practice I'd recommend, and this is something I do myself,

412
00:28:32.970 --> 00:28:37.049
[S06] is spending about five minutes before you do anything else, before you check your phone,

413
00:28:37.079 --> 00:28:41.529
[S06] before you let the world and just sitting with a version of you who already has what you want.

414
00:28:41.559 --> 00:28:47.619
[S06] And I want to be specific about what I mean, because it isn't visualization the, the way most people think of it.

415
00:28:47.650 --> 00:28:51.410
[S06] You're not trying to picture a mansion or a car or a perfect body here.

416
00:28:51.440 --> 00:28:56.170
[S06] You're thinking and feeling into a state, the internal experience of being the person

417
00:28:56.200 --> 00:28:58.250
[S06] who already lives that reality.

418
00:28:58.809 --> 00:29:03.690
[S06] What I mean by that is the particular combination of thoughts and feelings

419
00:29:03.720 --> 00:29:08.049
[S06] that would be present if your desired reality was already your current one.

420
00:29:08.410 --> 00:29:11.450
[S06] So for some people, that's a deep calm and a sense of certainty.

421
00:29:11.769 --> 00:29:14.650
[S06] For others, it can be just a warm confidence.

422
00:29:14.769 --> 00:29:17.809
[S06] For others, it's a quiet gratitude mixed with excitement.

423
00:29:18.289 --> 00:29:22.690
[S06] The exact flavor will be different for everyone, but the key is that it's felt,

424
00:29:22.730 --> 00:29:26.130
[S06] it's a felt experience in your body, not a picture in your mind

425
00:29:26.170 --> 00:29:29.210
[S06] or a sense, a sentence that you repeat like an affirmation.

426
00:29:29.240 --> 00:29:31.930
[S06] It's a, it's a felt experience.

427
00:29:32.210 --> 00:29:35.049
[S06] So you're really looking for a whole body experience here.

428
00:29:35.079 --> 00:29:38.650
[S06] Because that level of embodiment is what makes the signal strong enough

429
00:29:38.680 --> 00:29:40.579
[S06] for your nervous system to respond to it.

430
00:29:40.609 --> 00:29:45.410
[S06] And it helps to get really specific with yourself about what the thoughts and feelings actually are.

431
00:29:46.089 --> 00:29:47.890
[S06] And five minutes is genuinely enough.

432
00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:50.289
[S06] You don't need to like sit for an hour doing this.

433
00:29:50.309 --> 00:29:53.809
[S06] What matters is the quality of the thoughts and the feelings

434
00:29:53.849 --> 00:29:56.210
[S06] and how fully you let yourself drop into them.

435
00:29:56.849 --> 00:30:01.410
[S06] And if you do it consistently every morning, it becomes the state that you carry into the rest of your day,

436
00:30:01.440 --> 00:30:06.000
[S06] which means you're really running the inverted equation from the very start of your day.

437
00:30:06.690 --> 00:30:10.119
[S06] And consistency is the thing that makes this lot work long term.

438
00:30:10.150 --> 00:30:14.579
[S06] Because obviously, a single session feels nice, but doesn't really change much.

439
00:30:22.000 --> 00:30:23.920
[S07] A compounding investment.

440
00:30:23.950 --> 00:30:28.960
[S07] Each session adds a little bit to the total and over time those small deposits add up to

441
00:30:28.960 --> 00:30:33.549
[S07] a completely different internal state, which is going to produce obviously a completely

442
00:30:33.549 --> 00:30:36.720
[S07] different set of outputs in your external reality.

443
00:30:36.720 --> 00:30:41.289
[S07] Now, the compounding effect is why people who stick with this for a few months often

444
00:30:41.289 --> 00:30:46.359
[S07] describe the results as feeling almost sudden, even though the process was very gradual.

445
00:30:46.359 --> 00:30:52.069
[S07] And the reason this matters so much, the reason I'm spending this much time on it is because

446
00:30:52.069 --> 00:30:56.369
[S07] the thought and the feeling it produces are the actual variables that determine the output

447
00:30:56.369 --> 00:30:57.369
[S07] of the equation.

448
00:30:57.369 --> 00:31:01.220
[S07] Everything else, the money, the relationship, the health, the opportunities, those are all

449
00:31:01.220 --> 00:31:06.430
[S07] downstream of an internal state that was held consistently enough and long enough for

450
00:31:06.430 --> 00:31:08.930
[S07] reality to reorganize around it.

451
00:31:08.930 --> 00:31:13.319
[S07] And most people are focused entirely on the external things they want.

452
00:31:13.319 --> 00:31:17.549
[S07] The amount in the bank, maybe the relationship, the body, and they're trying to create those

453
00:31:17.549 --> 00:31:21.839
[S07] things directly through effort and strategy, which sometimes works but doesn't really

454
00:31:21.839 --> 00:31:27.400
[S07] last because the underlying input, your thoughts, feelings, and who you believe you are, haven't

455
00:31:27.400 --> 00:31:28.400
[S07] really changed.

456
00:31:28.400 --> 00:31:32.140
[S07] So the stuff is always downstream, it's always the effect.

457
00:31:32.140 --> 00:31:36.170
[S07] And the thoughts and the feelings are always the cause.

458
00:31:36.170 --> 00:31:39.470
[S07] And when you really get that, when it stops being a concept and becomes something you

459
00:31:39.470 --> 00:31:43.950
[S07] actually live by, then you stop chasing outcomes and you start managing your thinking and

460
00:31:43.950 --> 00:31:48.539
[S07] your internal state, which is the only lever that actually controls the output of the

461
00:31:48.539 --> 00:31:50.420
[S07] equation in a lasting way.

462
00:31:50.420 --> 00:31:54.029
[S07] And the only part that you can actually fully control.

463
00:31:54.029 --> 00:31:57.599
[S07] So when you sit down in the morning and do this practice, you're essentially giving

464
00:31:57.599 --> 00:32:00.750
[S07] reality a new set of instructions to solve for.

465
00:32:00.750 --> 00:32:05.329
[S07] You're plugging a different value into the input side of the equation and over time, as

466
00:32:05.329 --> 00:32:10.490
[S07] you hold that value more and more consistently, the output has to change because the input

467
00:32:10.490 --> 00:32:11.490
[S07] changed.

468
00:32:11.490 --> 00:32:13.990
[S07] And that's genuinely just how equations work, right?

469
00:32:13.990 --> 00:32:19.180
[S07] There's no version of this where you change one side and the other stays the same indefinitely.

470
00:32:19.180 --> 00:32:26.750
[S07] And that inevitability is something important and it's, you need to be able to trust because

471
00:32:26.750 --> 00:32:31.220
[S07] during the process, it can really feel uncertain, it can feel like nothing's happening, but

472
00:32:31.220 --> 00:32:32.920
[S07] the math is the math.

473
00:32:32.920 --> 00:32:37.799
[S07] If the input is different, then the output will eventually be different as well.

474
00:32:37.799 --> 00:32:42.730
[S07] And holding on to that understanding is what gets you through the difficult middle part.

475
00:32:42.730 --> 00:32:47.420
[S07] Once you've started flipping the variables, once you're regularly generating your internal

476
00:32:47.420 --> 00:32:52.240
[S07] state before your external world gives you a reason to, you're going to run into something

477
00:32:52.240 --> 00:32:57.720
[S07] that trips up almost everyone, and that's the lag between when the input changes and

478
00:32:57.720 --> 00:32:59.420
[S07] when the output catches up.

479
00:32:59.420 --> 00:33:02.799
[S07] So let's talk about holding the inversion through the lag.

480
00:33:02.799 --> 00:33:07.920
[S07] So this is the part where most people fall off.

481
00:33:07.920 --> 00:33:11.950
[S07] And honestly, it's the most important part to really understand because when you start

482
00:33:11.950 --> 00:33:17.339
[S07] running the inverted equation, when you genuinely shift your thinking and your internal state

483
00:33:17.339 --> 00:33:22.009
[S07] and start thinking and feeling differently on the inside, your external reality doesn't

484
00:33:22.009 --> 00:33:23.059
[S07] update right away.

485
00:33:23.059 --> 00:33:28.089
[S07] There's a delay, a gap, and that gap is where almost everyone gives up and really flips

486
00:33:28.089 --> 00:33:32.980
[S07] back to the default equation and they interpret the delay as proof that the inversion didn't

487
00:33:32.980 --> 00:33:33.980
[S07] work.

488
00:33:33.980 --> 00:33:37.230
[S07] Now, the lag makes sense if you think about the momentum involved.

489
00:33:37.230 --> 00:33:42.119
[S07] You might have spent five, 10, 20 years running the old equation in one direction, building

490
00:33:42.119 --> 00:33:46.869
[S07] up all this momentum through repetition, thinking certain thoughts, feeling certain

491
00:33:46.869 --> 00:33:49.839
[S07] feelings, acting from those patterns over and over again.

492
00:33:49.839 --> 00:33:53.589
[S07] And that momentum doesn't just stop the moment you decide to change.

493
00:33:53.589 --> 00:33:58.480
[S07] It can take some time to slow down and then reverse direction, which is completely normal

494
00:33:58.480 --> 00:33:59.980
[S07] and completely expected.

495
00:33:59.980 --> 00:34:01.809
[S07] It's logical as well.

496
00:34:01.809 --> 00:34:07.589
[S07] The old outputs you're seeing right now is the result of all that accumulated momentum

497
00:34:07.589 --> 00:34:11.449
[S07] and it's still being delivered to you because it was already in the pipeline, it was already

498
00:34:11.449 --> 00:34:13.559
[S07] queued up, already on its way.

499
00:34:13.559 --> 00:34:17.539
[S07] And nothing you do today can really recall it or speed up the transition.

500
00:34:17.539 --> 00:34:21.789
[S07] All you can do is keep putting new inputs into the equation and then wait for the new

501
00:34:21.789 --> 00:34:24.170
[S07] outputs to start arriving as well.

502
00:34:24.170 --> 00:34:26.760
[S07] And this is where patience becomes genuinely important.

503
00:34:26.760 --> 00:34:33.260
[S07] The lag can last days or weeks or sometimes longer, it can last years or months, depending

504
00:34:33.260 --> 00:34:36.090
[S07] on how much momentum the old equation really had.

505
00:34:36.090 --> 00:34:40.360
[S07] And during that time, you're essentially living in two realities at once.

506
00:34:40.360 --> 00:34:44.730
[S07] Your internal state says one thing and your external world says another.

507
00:34:44.730 --> 00:34:47.190
[S07] And that tension is uncomfortable.

508
00:34:47.190 --> 00:34:51.440
[S07] I get it completely, but it's also the clear sign that the inversion is working.

509
00:34:51.440 --> 00:34:55.880
[S07] And ask every successful person, they will tell you that this is the most important part

510
00:34:55.880 --> 00:35:00.849
[S07] of holding your thinking, holding your mindset in the right place, holding your thinking

511
00:35:05.510 --> 00:35:09.840
[S08] Now during the lag, the old reality is going to scream louder than it ever has.

512
00:35:09.929 --> 00:35:11.960
[S08] Because bills are still gonna come, right?

513
00:35:11.980 --> 00:35:15.190
[S08] There's still gonna be people acting in the same way with you.

514
00:35:15.210 --> 00:35:17.090
[S08] There's still gonna be setbacks that happen.

515
00:35:17.110 --> 00:35:21.369
[S08] And all of it is going to feel like evidence that nothing has really changed.

516
00:35:21.480 --> 00:35:26.469
[S08] But what's actually happening is that the old equation is finishing its print run.

517
00:35:26.780 --> 00:35:30.139
[S08] Those last pages from the previous job are still coming through the printer.

518
00:35:30.190 --> 00:35:35.579
[S08] And the worst thing you can do is look at those old pages and then conclude that your new equation didn't go through.

519
00:35:35.599 --> 00:35:37.860
[S08] Because it did, it's just waiting in line.

520
00:35:38.489 --> 00:35:42.829
[S08] So the old outputs that show up during the lag aren't new problems.

521
00:35:42.860 --> 00:35:45.789
[S08] They're old ones that were already in transit.

522
00:35:46.519 --> 00:35:50.530
[S08] They were created by the previous input and they're being delivered on schedule.

523
00:35:51.010 --> 00:35:52.869
[S08] You should have just expected them.

524
00:35:53.130 --> 00:35:56.599
[S08] And the fact that they're still arriving doesn't mean anything about what's coming next.

525
00:35:56.630 --> 00:35:58.360
[S08] That's even more important to realize.

526
00:35:58.429 --> 00:36:01.960
[S08] It just means that the delivery system has a built-in delay.

527
00:36:02.389 --> 00:36:08.059
[S08] The same way as when you order from Amazon or whatever, right?

528
00:36:08.079 --> 00:36:11.820
[S08] You pay and for a moment there, you have paid the money.

529
00:36:11.849 --> 00:36:18.409
[S08] It has exited, it has exited your bank account and you still haven't received the thing that you've ordered from Amazon.

530
00:36:18.449 --> 00:36:19.380
[S08] It's that delay.

531
00:36:20.079 --> 00:36:22.880
[S08] And this is genuinely the most misleading part of the whole process.

532
00:36:22.900 --> 00:36:29.829
[S08] Because your logical mind is going to look at the evidence and construct a very convincing argument that nothing has changed.

533
00:36:30.059 --> 00:36:31.429
[S08] And nothing is going to change.

534
00:36:31.909 --> 00:36:38.559
[S08] And that argument is going to feel reasonable and rational and most likely quote unquote realistic.

535
00:36:38.829 --> 00:36:45.000
[S08] But it's based entirely on old data, which makes it irrelevant to what's actually being created on the input side of the equation.

536
00:36:45.360 --> 00:36:48.199
[S08] And I want sugarcoated this part feels like a test.

537
00:36:48.230 --> 00:36:52.500
[S08] It feels like the universe, God, life, your mind, whatever you wanna call it.

538
00:36:52.699 --> 00:36:57.670
[S08] It's checking whether you really mean it or whether you're going to fold at the first sign of resistance.

539
00:36:57.860 --> 00:37:02.969
[S08] And while I don't really think of it as a cosmic text, the test exactly.

540
00:37:03.130 --> 00:37:05.170
[S08] The functional reality is the same.

541
00:37:05.199 --> 00:37:10.360
[S08] The lag is where your commitment to the inverted equation either holds or breaks.

542
00:37:10.690 --> 00:37:13.760
[S08] And that commitment is the only thing that really determines the outcome.

543
00:37:14.260 --> 00:37:22.369
[S08] Now, this, by the way, is what separates people who actually transform their lives from people who just keep cycling through the same old patterns.

544
00:37:23.130 --> 00:37:25.469
[S08] Because the information is really out there, right?

545
00:37:25.500 --> 00:37:27.969
[S08] Everyone has access to to these ideas now.

546
00:37:27.989 --> 00:37:35.030
[S08] But the people who break through are the ones who can hold the new input even when the old output is still showing up everywhere around them.

547
00:37:35.969 --> 00:37:39.269
[S08] That capacity to actually hold is the real skill.

548
00:37:39.599 --> 00:37:43.400
[S08] It's the thing that can be taught, that can't be taught through concepts alone.

549
00:37:43.420 --> 00:37:45.400
[S08] It has to be built through practice.

550
00:37:45.699 --> 00:37:53.340
[S08] And holding here means that when the old reality pushes back, when the lag delivers another piece of evidence from the old equation,

551
00:37:53.389 --> 00:37:57.460
[S08] from your old life, from your old way of thinking and feeling, you don't take the bait.

552
00:37:57.480 --> 00:38:01.630
[S08] You don't let it reset your thinking and your internal state back to the default.

553
00:38:01.860 --> 00:38:03.389
[S08] You just acknowledge what's happening.

554
00:38:03.420 --> 00:38:05.360
[S08] You feel whatever you feel for a moment.

555
00:38:05.510 --> 00:38:10.630
[S08] And then you consciously return to the chosen thoughts and emotional signature you set in step two.

556
00:38:10.659 --> 00:38:12.269
[S08] Because that's the input that matters.

557
00:38:12.380 --> 00:38:20.070
[S08] And every time you return to it after a disruption, you're actually strengthening the, strengthening the inverted equation rather than weakening it.

558
00:38:20.730 --> 00:38:25.869
[S08] So each return to your chosen state after a disruption is actually making the inversion stronger.

559
00:38:25.889 --> 00:38:28.400
[S08] Because you're not just maintaining the new input.

560
00:38:28.530 --> 00:38:33.800
[S08] You're proving to your nervous system that this state can survive contact with contradictory evidence,

561
00:38:33.849 --> 00:38:38.869
[S08] which builds the resilience that makes each subsequent disruption easier to handle.

562
00:38:39.230 --> 00:38:45.760
[S08] So the lag period, as uncomfortable as it is, is actually the part of the process where the most growth happens.

563
00:38:46.000 --> 00:38:52.300
[S08] Because it's where you build the capacity to hold an internal state independently of external circumstances.

564
00:38:52.570 --> 00:38:55.099
[S08] And that capacity is the whole game, right?

565
00:38:55.159 --> 00:39:00.300
[S08] Once you have it, the inversion becomes self-sustaining and the external changes follow naturally.

566
00:39:00.320 --> 00:39:06.369
[S08] And this is the, this, this capacity, the skill of being able to control your thoughts and control your feelings,

567
00:39:06.699 --> 00:39:15.530
[S08] is really one of the most underrated, I think, skills to success, really, in any field, not just financial success.

568
00:39:16.329 --> 00:39:20.070
[S08] And I want to stress again that this is pretty mechanical.

569
00:39:20.300 --> 00:39:22.130
[S08] It's just the way the system works.

570
00:39:22.570 --> 00:39:24.670
[S08] There's a delay between cause and effect.

571
00:39:24.769 --> 00:39:26.869
[S08] The old outputs need time to clear.

572
00:39:26.929 --> 00:39:31.670
[S08] And your job is during that time is simply to not flip the equation back to default.

573
00:39:31.690 --> 00:39:33.800
[S08] That's it. You don't need to do anything else.

574
00:39:34.170 --> 00:39:38.599
[S08] You just need to hold your position and keep feeding the new input into the equation.

575
00:39:39.429 --> 00:39:42.800
[S08] And the more systematically you approach this, the easier it gets.

576
00:39:42.829 --> 00:39:47.699
[S08] Meaning, if you have a clear morning practice, like we talked about in step two,

577
00:39:48.030 --> 00:39:52.170
[S08] and you have the equation check running a few times throughout the day from step one,

578
00:39:52.760 --> 00:39:56.070
[S08] you've basically built a system that supports the inversion automatically.

579
00:39:56.599 --> 00:39:59.329
[S08] So you're not really relying on willpower anymore.

580
00:39:59.670 --> 00:40:05.269
[S08] You have actual practices in place that keep the new input flowing even on difficult days.

581
00:40:06.300 --> 00:40:11.849
[S09] And that's why the three steps work together as a system rather than as an isolated technique.

582
00:40:12.119 --> 00:40:15.610
[S09] Because step one gives you the awareness to cash the default equation.

583
00:40:15.639 --> 00:40:18.480
[S09] Step two gives you the practice for setting the new input.

584
00:40:18.840 --> 00:40:24.449
[S09] And then step three is really about maintaining that new input through the period where the old output is still visible.

585
00:40:24.719 --> 00:40:26.460
[S09] And each step supports the other two.

586
00:40:27.150 --> 00:40:34.650
[S09] So the practical technique for really getting through the lag is what I call the lag reframe.

587
00:40:35.340 --> 00:40:43.340
[S09] And it goes like this, whenever all the reality pushes back, whenever something shows up that looks like proof that nothing is really changing.

588
00:40:44.099 --> 00:40:51.570
[S09] You recognize it for what it is, old output, already finished, already irrelevant to what you're actually building right now.

589
00:40:51.840 --> 00:40:57.179
[S09] And then instead of engaging with it, you bring your attention back to the internal state you set in step two.

590
00:40:57.510 --> 00:41:04.889
[S09] You reconnect with that feeling, to the thoughts, you hold it and you let the old output pass through without giving it any more of your energy.

591
00:41:05.699 --> 00:41:13.739
[S09] Now, the reason this works as a technique is because it gives your mind something specific to do in the moment of disruption.

592
00:41:13.860 --> 00:41:19.920
[S09] Instead of just trying to not react, which is vague and hard to execute, you're giving yourself a concrete reframe

593
00:41:20.159 --> 00:41:22.500
[S09] that puts the old output in context.

594
00:41:22.650 --> 00:41:25.650
[S09] And that context immediately takes the emotional charge out of it.

595
00:41:25.820 --> 00:41:29.070
[S09] You're no longer interpreting it as current evidence.

596
00:41:29.130 --> 00:41:33.539
[S09] You're interpreting it as old data that's just being cleared away.

597
00:41:34.800 --> 00:41:38.550
[S09] So the reframe can be almost immediate once you practice it a few times.

598
00:41:38.670 --> 00:41:44.760
[S09] To the point where you see an old pattern showing up and your first thought is just old stuff.

599
00:41:45.300 --> 00:41:46.409
[S09] And you just move on.

600
00:41:47.010 --> 00:41:51.269
[S09] So it's simple enough to remember and use even when you're stressed, which is exactly when you need it most.

601
00:41:51.269 --> 00:41:57.659
[S09] So keep it in your back pocket and use it every time the lag tries to pull you back into the old equation.

602
00:41:58.320 --> 00:42:05.340
[S09] Now, after you use the reframe, the redirect back to your chosen thoughts and emotional state is really the critical second step.

603
00:42:05.340 --> 00:42:10.050
[S09] Because the reframe alone will of course just neutralize that old trigger.

604
00:42:10.409 --> 00:42:12.030
[S09] But it doesn't generate any new input.

605
00:42:12.030 --> 00:42:19.530
[S09] So you need to actively bring your attention back to the thoughts and the feelings from your morning practice, even just for 10 or 15 seconds.

606
00:42:20.099 --> 00:42:23.360
[S09] It doesn't need to be a long process in the moment, just a quick reconnection.

607
00:42:24.139 --> 00:42:32.130
[S09] Just a brief dropping in to those thoughts and feelings of certainty or calm or whatever your cognitive and emotional signature was.

608
00:42:32.550 --> 00:42:34.559
[S09] Just enough to reestablish the signal.

609
00:42:34.980 --> 00:42:41.670
[S09] And each time you do this, each time you reframe and redirect, you're stacking another data point in favor of the new equation.

610
00:42:41.849 --> 00:42:45.780
[S09] And those data points accumulate into a new normal, a new baseline.

611
00:42:45.780 --> 00:42:48.480
[S09] And eventually the lag just ends, right?

612
00:42:48.510 --> 00:42:50.699
[S09] And the new output starts showing up in your life.

613
00:42:51.539 --> 00:42:56.250
[S09] So the question you want to be asking yourself during the lag isn't, has my reality changed yet?

614
00:42:56.550 --> 00:43:01.860
[S09] Because that's, that's as if you're asking every 10 minutes, are we there yet?

615
00:43:02.429 --> 00:43:08.610
[S09] And that question just keeps you focused on the output, which is exactly the, the wrong place to look during this phase.

616
00:43:08.639 --> 00:43:10.710
[S09] The real question is, have I changed?

617
00:43:11.400 --> 00:43:20.130
[S09] Because in any endeavor where you want, you, you aim to be successful, whether that's in sports or business or whatever.

618
00:43:20.309 --> 00:43:24.300
[S09] At the end of the day, the biggest, the biggest results come from you changing.

619
00:43:24.360 --> 00:43:29.250
[S09] The whole process, the whole journey is you changing as a person.

620
00:43:29.610 --> 00:43:35.369
[S09] And the shift in your external world is always a downstream consequence of the shift in you, right?

621
00:43:35.460 --> 00:43:42.480
[S09] And if you're genuinely holding a different internal state, if you're different and a different person in terms of your thoughts and your feelings.

622
00:43:43.050 --> 00:43:47.550
[S09] If you're running the inverted equation consistently, well, the external changes will follow.

623
00:43:47.550 --> 00:43:49.679
[S09] They just have to, because it's an equation.

624
00:43:50.400 --> 00:43:54.599
[S09] And that internal shift is the thing to measure yourself by during the lag period.

625
00:43:54.599 --> 00:44:00.539
[S09] Because it's the only metric that is actually within your control and the only one that really predicts the outcome.

626
00:44:00.869 --> 00:44:08.789
[S09] So instead of actually checking your bank account every day, hoping to see a change, which is really just running the default equation again.

627
00:44:09.269 --> 00:44:12.210
[S09] Check your thinking, check your internal state, your emotional state.

628
00:44:12.539 --> 00:44:15.960
[S09] Check whether you're holding the new input, check whether your baseline has shifted.

629
00:44:16.199 --> 00:44:19.949
[S09] And if it has, you're on track regardless of what the external evidence says.

630
00:44:20.400 --> 00:44:24.119
[S09] So during the lag, you don't really have external proof yet.

631
00:44:24.150 --> 00:44:28.349
[S09] All you have is the internal shift and your understanding of the equation.

632
00:44:29.000 --> 00:44:33.360
[S09] And that has to be enough for a while, which is uncomfortable, but also kind of beautiful.

633
00:44:33.539 --> 00:44:42.480
[S09] It means that you're really building something from the inside out, which is the only way anything real can be built and anything lasting can be built.

634
00:44:43.429 --> 00:44:49.739
[S09] Because like we've been saying throughout this whole training, your current reality is just a printout of a previous internal state.

635
00:44:50.579 --> 00:44:54.659
[S09] So when the internal state changes, the printout has to change as well.

636
00:44:55.349 --> 00:44:59.519
[S09] There's no version of this where the input shifts and the output stays the same forever.

637
00:44:59.610 --> 00:45:01.590
[S09] The equation has to balance.

638
00:45:03.449 --> 00:45:07.679
[S09] And it will, your only job is really to hold the new input steady until it does.

639
00:45:08.090 --> 00:45:09.280
[S10] That's it.

640
00:45:09.309 --> 00:45:11.420
[S10] So with that said, let's cover the review.

641
00:45:11.449 --> 00:45:14.280
[S10] We talked about the overview, the backwards equation,

642
00:45:14.309 --> 00:45:16.880
[S10] seeing the equation, flipping the variables,

643
00:45:16.909 --> 00:45:18.960
[S10] holding the inversion through the lag,

644
00:45:18.989 --> 00:45:21.639
[S10] the review, and finally your action items for the day

645
00:45:21.670 --> 00:45:22.800
[S10] or the next few days.

646
00:45:22.829 --> 00:45:25.599
[S10] First, start running the equation check today.

647
00:45:25.630 --> 00:45:28.400
[S10] Pause a few times throughout your day and ask yourself,

648
00:45:28.429 --> 00:45:30.639
[S10] "Am I reacting to my reality right now?

649
00:45:30.670 --> 00:45:32.280
[S10] Or am I creating it?"

650
00:45:32.309 --> 00:45:34.119
[S10] And then use that question as your anchor

651
00:45:34.150 --> 00:45:38.519
[S10] for building the awareness that makes the inversion possible.

652
00:45:38.550 --> 00:45:40.880
[S10] Then begin your morning calibration tomorrow,

653
00:45:40.909 --> 00:45:42.639
[S10] five minutes before you touch your phone,

654
00:45:42.670 --> 00:45:45.760
[S10] sitting with the emotional and cognitive signature

655
00:45:45.789 --> 00:45:48.880
[S10] of the version of you who already has what you want,

656
00:45:48.909 --> 00:45:51.400
[S10] thinking and feeling into that state fully,

657
00:45:51.429 --> 00:45:54.880
[S10] and then letting it set the tone for your entire day.

658
00:45:54.909 --> 00:45:59.360
[S10] Then finally, hold the thoughts and the feelings, right?

659
00:45:59.389 --> 00:46:02.119
[S10] When the old reality pushes back, and it will,

660
00:46:02.150 --> 00:46:03.360
[S10] just expect it.

661
00:46:03.389 --> 00:46:05.679
[S10] Use the lag reframe to put it in context.

662
00:46:05.710 --> 00:46:07.599
[S10] Remind yourself that what you're seeing

663
00:46:07.630 --> 00:46:11.840
[S10] is just an old, printout job finishing.

664
00:46:11.869 --> 00:46:13.639
[S10] And then just redirect your attention

665
00:46:13.670 --> 00:46:16.280
[S10] to your chosen thinking and internal state,

666
00:46:16.309 --> 00:46:19.559
[S10] and trust that the new equation is already processing.

667
00:46:19.590 --> 00:46:20.920
[S10] With that said, I hope you enjoyed this.

668
00:46:20.949 --> 00:46:22.480
[S10] I hope it brought a lot of value.

669
00:46:22.510 --> 00:46:23.920
[S10] If it did, make sure to like the video,

670
